  data: {
    LLM: 'A hand proceeds in four main stages: (1) bid for right to use stock; highest bidder pays bid amount split to opponents and exchanges by discarding and taking stock cards; (2) vie for Ruff, the highest valued suit total in hand (aces 11, courts 10, numerals face value), with betting actions similar to poker; (3) declare Mournivals (four of a kind) and Gleeks (three of a kind) for fixed payments from opponents; (4) play 12 tricks, eldest leading first trick, following suit when possible, with trump from turn-up card. Trick stage adds point settlement around trick count and honour values. Historical sources disagree on some details, so rule variants must be table-agreed before play.',
    Player: 'A hand proceeds in four main stages: (1) bid for right to use stock; highest bidder pays bid amount split to opponents and exchanges by discarding and taking stock cards; (2) vie for Ruff, the highest valued suit total in hand (aces 11, courts 10, numerals face value), with betting actions similar to poker; (3) declare Mournivals (four of a kind) and Gleeks (three of a kind) for fixed payments from opponents; (4) play 12 tricks, eldest leading first trick, following suit when possible, with trump from turn-up card. Trick stage adds point settlement around trick count and honour values. Historical sources disagree on some details, so rule variants must be table-agreed before play.',
    objective: 'Profit across phases by winning stock bid value lines, ruff vie pot, set declarations, and trick-stage point settlement.',
    gameplay: 'A hand proceeds in four main stages: (1) bid for right to use stock; highest bidder pays bid amount split to opponents and exchanges by discarding and taking stock cards; (2) vie for Ruff, the highest valued suit total in hand (aces 11, courts 10, numerals face value), with betting actions similar to poker; (3) declare Mournivals (four of a kind) and Gleeks (three of a kind) for fixed payments from opponents; (4) play 12 tricks, eldest leading first trick, following suit when possible, with trump from turn-up card. Trick stage adds point settlement around trick count and honour values. Historical sources disagree on some details, so rule variants must be table-agreed before play.',
    keyRules: [
      'A gleek is three of a kind and a mournival is four of a kind.',
      'Ruff compares best suit-point total, not generic hand rank.',
      'Trick phase is fixed at 12 tricks with follow-suit requirement.',
      'Extant reconstructions differ on specific edge rules; session must declare which reconstruction is authoritative.',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
